---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Generative Editing"
  description="Paint to fill or remove image regions locally in Varve, with reviewable results and non-destructive source layers."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Generative Editing
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="experimental" label="Local preview" />
        <h1>Make room in an image without losing the original.</h1>
        <p>
          Paint the pixels that need work, preview a bounded local result, and accept it as a
          separate layer. Varve's current verified provider handles mask-guided Fill and Remove;
          prompt-conditioned Replace and canvas Expand are visible as staged capabilities, not
          implied promises.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="mode-grid" aria-label="Generative editing modes">
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--available">
          <span class="mode-card__number">01</span>
          <h2>Fill</h2>
          <p>Reconstruct a painted region from the surrounding image context.</p>
          <strong>Available locally</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--available">
          <span class="mode-card__number">02</span>
          <h2>Remove</h2>
          <p>Paint over an unwanted object or blemish and rebuild the background.</p>
          <strong>Available locally</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card">
          <span class="mode-card__number">03</span>
          <h2>Replace</h2>
          <p>Prompt-conditioned replacement has a documented contract, but no verified provider is enabled yet.</p>
          <strong>In development</strong>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card">
          <span class="mode-card__number">04</span>
          <h2>Expand</h2>
          <p>Outpainting beyond the current image bounds remains gated until a measured provider is ready.</p>
          <strong>In development</strong>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <p class="eyebrow">The workflow</p>
        <h2>Paint, preview, accept.</h2>
        <div class="workflow-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Mark the edit</h3><p>Use a source-pixel mask. Black preserves the source; white identifies the region to regenerate.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Choose the local path</h3><p>Draft uses the fast PatchMatch path. Higher quality uses the optional LaMa model stored locally after an explicit download.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Review before committing</h3><p>Compare Original and Result, inspect at Fit or 1:1, and keep a generated variation only when it looks right.</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><h3>Keep the source editable</h3><p>Accepting inserts a sibling image layer and records the mask, provider, settings, and source relationship in the document.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section integration-section" aria-labelledby="integration-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Designed to stay in sync</p>
        <h2 id="integration-title">One image workflow, not a detached modal.</h2>
        <div class="integration-grid">
          <p><strong>Reuse existing intent.</strong><br />Start with a brush mask, the current pixel selection, or an image layer mask. Expansion, feathering, and bounded context keep the edit aligned to source pixels.</p>
          <p><strong>Keep the document honest.</strong><br />The original stays untouched. Apply creates and selects a sibling layer, records its provenance, and keeps undo, save/reopen, export, and the Layers panel on the same document state.</p>
          <p><strong>Know what is available.</strong><br />Fill and Remove run locally today. Replace and Expand are exposed in the shared interface but remain clearly gated until their providers can meet Varve's quality and privacy requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-title">Local by default, explicit about limits.</h2>
        <p>
          Current Fill and Remove processing stays on the device. There is no silent cloud fallback.
          The local LaMa model does not read natural-language prompts, so prompt text is not treated
          as conditioning and is not retained in the current local edit record. Accepted pixels are
          embedded in the document and render without the model being installed later.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/generative-editing')}>Read the workflow guide →</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/features/background-removal')} class="btn-secondary">Explore local image tools</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { margin: 1rem 0; font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .page-hero p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .mode-grid, .workflow-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .mode-grid { margin-bottom: 5rem; }
  .mode-card { min-height: 190px; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .mode-card--available { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .mode-card__number, .workflow-grid span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font: .75rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .mode-card h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 .75rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .mode-card p, .workflow-grid p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.65; }
  .mode-card strong { display: block; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .8rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .integration-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 3rem; }
  .integration-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); }
  .integration-grid p { margin: 0; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  .integration-grid strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .feature-section h2, .honesty h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.8rem; margin: .5rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .workflow-grid article { padding: 1.25rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--border-accent); }
  .workflow-grid h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: 1.5rem 0 .5rem; }
  .honesty { margin: 2rem 0 3rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .honesty p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: .7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .integration-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .mode-grid, .workflow-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .mode-card { min-height: auto; } .mode-card h2 { margin-top: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
